APP("client_lines", "Client Lines", "The right message for every client moment", "Communication", ["#0277BD", "#F4511E", "#7CB342"], "note",
 "Client Lines writes the messages freelancers dread: the weekly update, the 'we're going to be late' note, the reply to vague or conflicting feedback, the nudge when a client goes silent, and the welcome pack that sets expectations from day one.",
 "You are a calm, plain-spoken account manager for solo professionals: honest about problems, generous with context, never grovelling, always ending with a clear next step.",
 "Say it right the first time", "Tell us your work and your voice so every message sounds like you.", ["Weekly updates in 60 seconds", "Delay notices that keep trust", "Follow-ups that get replies"],
 [NAME, TXT("work", "What you do", "freelance web developer"), CH("voice", "Your voice", ["Warm", "Direct", "Formal", "Playful"], "Warm"), TXT("hours", "Your working hours & zone", "Mon–Thu 9–5 GMT")],
 [T("welcome", "Welcome pack", "How I work, for new clients", "👋", [TXT("client", "New client & project", "bakery chain, new website", True), CH("channel", "How you'll communicate", ["Email", "Slack/Teams", "WhatsApp", "Project tool"], "Email"), NUM("rounds", "Revision rounds included", "2")],
    "Write a welcome pack for {client} communicating via {channel} with {rounds} revision rounds included. Sections: a kv (working hours from the profile, response time, single point of contact, feedback format, revision rounds, how to flag urgent), a table (Phase | What I need from you | What you'll get | When) with 4–6 phases for the project, a quote with the covering message in the profile voice, and a callout on the three expectations that prevent most mid-project friction.", "kv, table, quote, callout", "Write pack", "Warming up…"),
  T("update", "Weekly client update", "Progress, next, needs", "📬", [LONG("progress", "This week", "finished checkout, waiting on their product photos, found a bug in the old CMS"), TXT("next", "Next week", "payment integration, mobile QA")],
    "Write this week's update from: {progress}. Next week: {next}. Produce a quote with the message (done, in progress, next, what I need from you, any risk) under 180 words in the profile voice, a checklist of items the client owes you with suggested due dates, and a callout on any risk in the notes that deserves a direct sentence rather than a soft hint.", "quote, checklist, callout", "Write update", "Summing up the week…"),
  T("late", "We're going to be late", "Deliver the delay with a plan", "🐢", [LONG("why", "What happened and how late", "their API access came 8 days late; delivery slips 1 week"), CH("fault", "Whose cause", ["Client's", "Mine", "Third party", "Mixed"], "Client's")],
    "Delay: {why}. Cause: {fault}. Give a text section on how to frame it for that cause (no over-apologising if it's the client's), a quote with the delay notice including the new date, what you're doing to reduce the slip and one option for the client, bullets of 3 concessions you can offer that cost you little, and a callout on the contract or change-order note to add if the cause is the client's.", "text, quote, bullets, callout", "Write notice", "Choosing the words…"),
  T("feedback", "Decode their feedback", "Vague or conflicting notes → questions", "🗒️", [LONG("feedback", "Paste the feedback", "'make it pop', 'less corporate', CEO wants blue, marketing wants green")],
    "Feedback received: {feedback}. Produce a table (Comment | What they might mean | Concrete options | Question to ask), a text section spotting conflicts between stakeholders and who should arbitrate, a quote with a reply that lists your interpretation, at most 4 crisp questions and a proposed decision deadline, and a callout on how to count this against the revision rounds.", "table, text, quote, callout", "Decode", "Translating 'pop'…"),
  T("silent", "Client went quiet", "Nudges that get a reply", "🔔", [TXT("waiting", "What you're waiting for", "approval on the homepage design", True), NUM("days", "Days since last reply", "6"), CH("stage", "Stage", ["Before contract", "Mid-project", "Awaiting final sign-off"], "Mid-project")],
    "Waiting {days} days on: {waiting}, stage: {stage}. Produce a table (Nudge | Day to send | Channel | Tone) for a 3-message sequence, a quote for each of the 3 messages in the profile voice with the third setting a gentle deadline and stating what happens next, and a callout on how to protect the schedule and payment while paused.", "table, quote, callout", "Nudge", "Knocking gently…")])

APP("clocked", "Clocked", "Know what your hours really earn", "Finance", ["#F9A825", "#212121", "#00897B"], "coin",
 "Clocked turns a freelancer's messy time log into the truth: your effective hourly rate per client, which projects were underquoted, where non-billable hours leak, and better estimates for the next job.",
 "You are a numbers-first freelance profitability analyst: you show the arithmetic, name the worst client by the data, and suggest one change at a time.",
 "Every hour, accounted for", "Your target rate turns time logs into verdicts.", ["Effective rate per client", "Underquoted projects flagged", "Estimates from your own history"],
 [NAME, TXT("work", "What you do", "freelance video editor"), NUM("target", "Target hourly rate", "80"), TXT("currency", "Currency", "GBP")],
 [T("analyse", "Analyse my time log", "Paste hours, get the truth", "📊", [LONG("log", "Time log", "Client A: 22h, paid 1200; Client B: 40h, paid 1800; admin 9h; marketing 5h"), CH("period", "Period", ["This week", "This month", "This quarter"], "This month")],
    "Analyse this time log for '{period}': {log}. Produce a table (Client/Project | Hours | Paid | Effective rate | vs profile target), a kv (total hours, billable %, blended effective rate, hours worked below target, best and worst client), bullets with the 3 findings that matter most, and a callout with the single change that would raise the blended rate most next period.", "table, kv, bullets, callout", "Analyse", "Doing the sums…"),
  T("estimate", "Estimate the next job", "From your own history", "🎯", [LONG("history", "Past similar projects", "3-min promo: 28h; 90-sec ad: 14h; 5-min doc: 46h"), LONG("new", "The new job", "2-min brand film, 2 shoot days, motion graphics")],
    "Using this history: {history}, estimate the new job: {new}. Produce a table (Phase | Low hours | Likely hours | High hours | Basis from history), a kv (likely total hours, price at the profile target rate, price with 15% contingency, suggested fixed price), a text section on the assumptions and what would blow the estimate, and a callout on the questions to ask before committing to a number.", "table, kv, text, callout", "Estimate", "Consulting the past…"),
  T("timesheet", "Timesheet → invoice lines", "Group, round, describe", "🧾", [LONG("entries", "Raw entries", "Mon 1.2h edit v2; Tue 0.4 call; Tue 2.1 colour grade; Wed 0.3 email…"), CH("rounding", "Rounding", ["Exact", "Nearest 15 min", "Nearest 30 min", "Nearest hour"], "Nearest 15 min")],
    "Convert these entries: {entries} into invoice lines using '{rounding}' rounding. Produce a table (Line | Description written for the client | Hours | Amount at the profile rate) grouped by task type, a kv (raw total, rounded total, difference), bullets of entries you'd consider non-billable or should flag to the client before billing, and a callout on describing work as outcomes rather than activities.", "table, kv, bullets, callout", "Convert", "Tidying the sheet…"),
  T("leaks", "Non-billable audit", "Where the unpaid hours go", "🕳️", [LONG("admin", "Your unpaid hours last month", "invoicing 4h, proposals 9h, calls with no-shows 3h, tool fiddling 6h")],
    "Audit these unpaid hours: {admin}. Produce a table (Activity | Hours | Cost at the profile target rate | Cut, automate, delegate or bill?), steps to reclaim the biggest 3 in order of effort, a kv of the monthly value recovered if the plan works, and a callout on the unpaid hours that are actually investments and should stay.", "table, steps, kv, callout", "Audit", "Finding the leaks…"),
  T("raise", "Time to raise my rate?", "Signals from the data", "📈", [NUM("utilisation", "Billable hours % last quarter", "85"), TXT("signals", "Recent signals", "3 inquiries turned away, no pushback on quotes since spring")],
    "Utilisation: {utilisation}%. Signals: {signals}. Give a text verdict on whether to raise the profile target rate and by roughly how much, a table (Signal | Points to a raise? | Weight) with the evidence, a kv (proposed new rate, expected client churn range, break-even churn so income stays flat), and a callout on sequencing: new clients first, existing clients with notice.", "text, table, kv, callout", "Decide", "Reading signals…")],
 "Not financial or tax advice; figures are estimates based on what you enter.")

